      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we start with the given that \\(\\alpha\\) is inversely proportional to \\(\\beta\\). This relationship can be expressed mathematically as:\n\n\\[\n\\alpha = \\frac{k}{\\beta}\n\\]\n\nwhere \\(k\\) is a constant of proportionality. We need to determine the value of \\(k\\). We know from the problem statement that when \\(\\alpha = 4\\) and \\(\\beta = 9\\), the relation holds perfectly. So we can substitute these values into our equation to find \\(k\\):\n\n\\[\n4 = \\frac{k}{9}\n\\]\n\nNext, we solve for \\(k\\) by multiplying both sides by 9:\n\n\\[\nk = 4 \\times 9 = 36\n\\]\n\nNow that we have the constant \\(k\\), we can use it to find \\(\\alpha\\) when \\(\\beta = -72\\). We substitute \\(\\beta = -72\\) and the value of \\(k\\) into the equation:\n\n\\[\n\\alpha = \\frac{36}{-72}\n\\]\n\nSimplifying the fraction, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\alpha = -\\frac{1}{2}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(\\alpha\\) when \\(\\beta = -72\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-\\frac{1}{2}}\n\\]",
